{"name":"Peruvian Lily","hex":"#cd7db5","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lily","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several flowers in the genus Lilium of the family Liliaceae, which includes a great many ornamental species.","Any of several species of herbaceous flower which may or may not resemble the genus Lilium in some way, and which are not closely related to it or each other."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["White ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lily"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alstroemeria","blocks":[{"text":"Alstroemeria, commonly called the Peruvian lily or lily of the Incas, is a genus of flowering plants in the family Alstroemeriaceae. They are all native to South America, although some have become naturalized in the United States, Mexico, Australia, New Zealand, Madeira and the Canary Islands. Almost all of the species are restricted to one of two distinct centers of diversity: one in central Chile and southern Argentina, the other in eastern Brazil. Species of Alstroemeria from Patagonia are winter-growing plants, while those of Brazil are summer growing. All are long-lived perennials except A. graminea, a diminutive annual from the Atacama Desert of Chile."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Alstroemeria_aurantiaca.jpg/330px-Alstroemeria_aurantiaca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alstroemeria","wikidata":"Q917833"},{"title":"Lilium","blocks":[{"text":"Lilium is a genus of herbaceous flowering plants growing from bulbs, all with large and often prominent flowers. Lilies are a group of flowering plants which are important in culture and literature in much of the world. Most species are native to the Northern Hemisphere and their range is temperate climates and extends into the subtropics. Many other plants have \"lily\" in their common names, but do not belong to the same genus and are therefore not true lilies. True lilies are known to be highly toxic to cats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Lilium_candidum_1.jpg/330px-Lilium_candidum_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilium","wikidata":"Q5194627"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Alstroemeria_aurantiaca.jpg/500px-Alstroemeria_aurantiaca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Alstroemeria_aurantiaca.jpg/1280px-Alstroemeria_aurantiaca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Alstroemeria_aurantiaca.jpg/500px-Alstroemeria_aurantiaca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlstroemeria_aurantiaca.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Alstroemeria.jpg/500px-Alstroemeria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Alstroemeria.jpg/1280px-Alstroemeria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Alstroemeria.jpg/500px-Alstroemeria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alstroemeria × hybrida in the Lalbagh Botanical Gardens","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlstroemeria.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Alstroemeria_aurea_%27Saturne%27.jpg/500px-Alstroemeria_aurea_%27Saturne%27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Alstroemeria_aurea_%27Saturne%27.jpg/